  "statementTechnical": "A constraint C restricts a possibility space, yielding a permitted set P. Where |P| > 1, C is exhausted and no further constraint collapses P to a single member without either (a) reducing |P| to 1, in which case no selection occurred and the outcome was determined, or (b) introducing a non-constraint term. Selection — the map P → p_i for |P| > 1 — is therefore not a constraint operation. Candidate selectors reduce to law (fails by (a)), chance (a measure over P is itself a constraint and does not draw), or agent (the residual: a term capable of resolving P without being compelled by C). The operation appears at three scales sharing four invariants: multi-valued permitted set, single actual outcome, agent-requiring resolution, irreversibility with cost. Cosmological actualization, quantum measurement (Law 7), and moral regime selection (W in Laws 1-8) are structurally isomorphic under this description.",

  "statementPlain": "Rules say what is allowed. They never pick. Building code has never built a house — it only says what a legal house must satisfy. If two outcomes are both allowed, the rules have said everything they can say and both are still standing. Something has to pick one. That picking is not a rule, and adding more rules will never produce it. The same picking shows up three times: one universe out of the many the laws permit, one measurement outcome out of many, one choice out of two open to a person. Each time: many possible, one actual, no going back without paying. The framework already calls that W.",

  "mathematicalForm": "C: possibility space → P (permitted set). |P| > 1 ⟹ C exhausted. select: P → p_i requires term S ∉ C. cost(select) > 0. reverse(select) > cost(select).",

  "mathFormNormal": "P = {p1..pn}, n > 1, all permitted by C ; select(P) -> pi ; cost(select) > 0 ; reverse(select) requires cost > cost(select) ; C alone does not determine i",

  "axiomRoot": "https://faiththruphysics.com/claims/master-equation/01/000",

