  "falsificationCondition": "PRIMARY: exhibit selection of one actual from many permitted with no agent and no irreversible cost. SECONDARY: (1) a constraint that collapses a multi-member permitted set without an additional term; (2) a fourth candidate selector that is neither law, chance, nor agent; (3) demonstration that the three scales do not share the four invariants; (4) STRONGEST — demonstration that the permitted set is always single-membered, i.e. full determinism, in which case nothing is ever selected and the argument is vacuous.",

  "priorArt": "Leibniz 1714 (sufficient reason); Hawking 1988 ('what breathes fire into the equations'); Craig 1979- (Kalam, agent causation from a timeless cause); Swinburne (personal explanation). Contested by Krauss, Carroll, Hartle-Hawking no-boundary. Novelty claimed is narrow: formalization as a term in a working equation, the cross-scale isomorphism as a graded claim, and the type-error framing that makes it falsifiable rather than merely unsolved.",

